# Response headers for hosts that read a `_headers` file (Netlify). On Cloudflare Pages the
# _worker.js beside this file sets the same headers (Pages skips _headers when a worker is present).
# COOP + COEP make the page cross-origin isolated, so AppDatabaseFactory uses the WebWorker + OPFS
# SQLite driver and data survives a reload. Without them (GitHub Pages cannot send headers) the app
# falls back to an in-memory database. Same headers as webpack.config.d/dev-server-headers.js locally.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
